  "beats": [
    {
      "id": "B1",
      "shot": "SC_001",
      "audio_file": "audio/beats/B1.wav",
      "audio_sha256": "5886f05b108a936a496a91dd0b77dd7d0e89656e140563cba7cbbe373c0733ce",
      "start_seconds": 0.3,
      "duration": 8.11,
      "sentences": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "text": "In Babergh and Mid Suffolk, in eastern England, historic roofs do not all look alike.",
          "start": 0.3,
          "end": 5.18
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "text": "Some rise steeply. Others sit noticeably lower.",
          "start": 5.53,
          "end": 8.41
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "B2",
      "shot": "SC_002",
      "audio_file": "audio/beats/B2.wav",
      "audio_sha256": "a642c27c906d629a693812c427096c51e34a874c8ab3849af1fec8d30fc1322e",
      "start_seconds": 9.3,
      "duration": 13.62,
      "sentences": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "text": "Older timber-framed buildings here were probably roofed with thatch or oak shingles, depending on which materials were available.",
          "start": 9.3,
          "end": 16.23
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "text": "Longstraw thatch, the most traditional covering in these districts, is laid at a steep pitch of about fifty degrees.",
          "start": 16.58,
          "end": 22.92
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "B3",
      "shot": "SC_003",
      "audio_file": "audio/beats/B3.wav",
      "audio_sha256": "d8bd6f23e6a85e3c9a80da2ee198f1e20a8c442005fb1e8227acb0c95354c5c4",
      "start_seconds": 23.8,
      "duration": 8.97,
      "sentences": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "text": "Eventually, clay peg tiles replaced some of these thatched roofs.",
          "start": 23.8,
          "end": 27.66
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "text": "Plain clay tile roofs are fairly steep too, typically forty-five degrees or more.",
          "start": 28.01,
          "end": 32.77
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "B4",
      "shot": "SC_004",
      "audio_file": "audio/beats/B4.wav",
      "audio_sha256": "27855e8e64990d6516c3aee7a26d53b1e144649b9533cd8e017668c7db0bce04",
      "start_seconds": 33.633333,
      "duration": 15.84,
      "sentences": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "text": "Materials also began to travel further.",
          "start": 33.633333,
          "end": 35.983333
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "text": "From the eighteenth century, clay pantiles were used more commonly, as moving materials around the country became easier.",
          "start": 36.333333,
          "end": 43.203333
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "text": "In the nineteenth century, the railways meant that slate from Wales, Cornwall and Cumbria was often used here.",
          "start": 43.553333,
          "end": 49.473333
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "B5",
      "shot": "SC_005",
      "audio_file": "audio/beats/B5.wav",
      "audio_sha256": "bec2278619a3f763428e08253da6f863ab004d23c3722ded4bcc1611e4ec56bc",
      "start_seconds": 50.341667,
      "duration": 9.37,
      "sentences": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "text": "Slate behaves differently.",
          "start": 50.341667,
          "end": 52.041667
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "text": "Slate roofs here are usually pitched at around thirty degrees, and slate is more effective than smaller tiles at a lower pitch.",
          "start": 52.391667,
          "end": 59.711667
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "B6",
      "shot": "SC_006",
      "audio_file": "audio/beats/B6.wav",
      "audio_sha256": "c3509466578748af501bb18f4ca0a2c1bb28148baab4954678a8ec839e04d49a",
      "start_seconds": 60.591667,
      "duration": 11.85,
      "sentences": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "text": "Thatch, clay tile and slate each have a typical pitch.",
          "start": 60.591667,
          "end": 63.751667
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "text": "These are tendencies, not rules, and not every building followed the same path.",
          "start": 64.101667,
          "end": 68.631667
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "text": "But the pitch of an old roof can still be a clue to its covering.",
          "start": 68.981667,
          "end": 72.441667
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
